  m_Name: Object_41
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Engine Block (2)
  description: The Engine Block (2) is a large, elongated component situated at the
    middle-center-center of the engine, made of accent-yellow material. It serves
    as the main structural component of the engine, housing the cylinders, crankshaft,
    and camshaft, and providing a foundation for the engine's operation. Notably,
    the engine block's large size and elongated shape allow for a high power-to-weight
    ratio, enabling the engine to generate significant thrust while minimizing weight
    and maximizing fuel efficiency.
